Description:
A seminal study from Kuhn and Culhane documented 3 types of groups of homelessness populations as based on a study of the decade in New York and Philadelphia shelters: (1) transient, 80 percent of those using the shelter who had a single brief stay; 
(2) episodic, 10 percent of shelter users who had repeated but brief shelter stays; and 
(3) chronic, 10 percent of users who essentially spent each night in the shelter.
